---
source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
---
Stream the logs of one timeline of a run.

An Antithesis run is a tree of timelines. From one moment, Antithesis can send
different inputs, and each input starts a new branch. An input_hash names the
part of a branch from one input to the next. Each event has a moment: an
input_hash, and a vtime, the virtual time on that branch.

INPUT_HASH selects a path in the tree. The logs stream from the root, through
each earlier input_hash on the path, to the end of INPUT_HASH. INPUT_HASH is
often negative, such as `-123`; pass it as it is, with no `--` before it. Give
VTIME to end the stream at that moment, or --begin-vtime to start it later than
the root. A run in progress can extend INPUT_HASH, so it can return more logs
later. Find a moment with `runs properties --detail`, `runs events`,
`runs search`, or the failure moment of an incomplete run in `runs show`.

Each event also has a source and a payload: log output, an SDK assertion, a
fault, a container lifecycle change, or a test composer command.

Output: a `moment HASH` divider opens the events of each input_hash on the path,
from the root to INPUT_HASH. Each event under it renders on one line as
`VTIME [source] payload`, each event shape in its own concise form. VTIME is
truncated to fit its column, and a long source label ends in `…`. With --detail,
VTIME and the source print whole, and indented lines under an event give its
source location, as `@ file:function:line`, and the details that it carries,
such as an SDK assertion's details, as `details {...}`.

Add --json for machine-readable output. Each event prints as one JSON object on
its own line:
  snouty --json runs logs <run_id> <hash> | jq -r .moment.vtime

Usage: snouty runs logs [OPTIONS] <RUN_ID> <INPUT_HASH> [VTIME]

Arguments:
  <RUN_ID>
          Run ID

  <INPUT_HASH>
          Input hash at the end of the path to stream

  [VTIME]
          Virtual time of the moment to end the stream at; omit it to stream to
          the end of the input hash

Options:
      --begin-vtime <BEGIN_VTIME>
          Start from this virtual time instead of the root

  -d, --detail
          Detailed rendering: a full-width vtime on every line, source
          locations, and each event's attached details JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
